================================================================================
PLAN-EXPECTED CLASSIFICATION PHRASING
================================================================================

Under the AOU-LD-PIPELINE.md Section 12 R1 framing seeded into the M3
plan, the M3 LD R matrices satisfy the AoU egress classification of an
"Aggregate summary statistic" (no individual-level information; every
cell of the matrix is computed from ALL n >= 60k AFR participants -- and
>= 130k EUR participants on the parity panel -- so trivially clears the
n >= 20 cell-level suppression floor). The institutional NCSU-faculty
controlled-tier basis above preempts the per-data-class AoU support
letter the original plan acceptance criterion expected.

================================================================================
WHY NO AOU SUPPORT LETTER WAS ISSUED
================================================================================

The original AOU-LD-PIPELINE.md Section 12 R1 framing was conservative:
it anticipated that AoU might classify variant x variant LD matrices as
"derived individual-level data" requiring a custom egress letter before
any Dataproc spend. On Carter PI investigation 2026-04-28, the AoU
controlled-tier policy as actually administered for NCSU-faculty
accounts handles aggregate / derived statistics under the standard
egress-review pipeline (automated + manual reviewer at egress-request
time) and does NOT require a per-data-class custom letter for matrices
of this kind. The risk anticipated by Section 12 R1 is therefore
realized as a routine per-file egress review at Wave 4 production
fire, not as a Wave 1 hard gate.

